      "body": "## Overview\n\n`benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py` cannot tune `Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` (`Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration`): `get_model_params()` falls through to the default branch and fails on the nested text config.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The tuner runs on `Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8` and writes a config for the fused MoE kernel (E=64 per GPU with TEP8/DEP8, N=640, fp8 block [128,128]).\n- No behavior change for any other architecture: two names added to the branch that already handles `Qwen3VLMoe` and `Qwen3_5Moe`.\n\n## Validation\n\nBefore, on `main`:\n\n```\n$ python benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py --model Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 --tp-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel --dtype fp8_w8a8 --batch-size 1\nAttributeError: 'Qwen4ExpTextConfig' object has no attribute 'intermediate_size'. Did you mean: 'moe_intermediate_size'?\n```\n\nAfter, same command on this branch (8x H100 SXM, driver 580.173, Triton 3.8.0):\n\n```\nBatch size: 1, config: {'BLOCK_SIZE_M': 16, 'BLOCK_SIZE_N': 64, 'BLOCK_SIZE_K': 128, 'GROUP_SIZE_M': 1, 'SPLIT_K': 1, 'num_warps': 4, 'num_stages': 4}\nKernel time: 36.36 us\n```\n\nA full `--tune` run on the same node produced\n`E=64,N=640,device_name=NVIDIA_H100_80GB_HBM3,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json`.\nServing the FP8 checkpoint with that config via `VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER` (DP4 x TP2 + EP, MTP, long multi-turn agentic requests at 128 concurrent streams) raised prompt throughput from 124k to 137k tok/s and end-to-end agent turns/min by 9%; without the file vLLM logs `Using default MoE config. Performance might be sub-optimal!` for this shape. The config itself is not part of this PR.\n\n## Details\n\nQwen4Exp stores `num_experts`, `num_experts_per_tok`, `moe_intermediate_size` and `hidden_size` under `text_config`, the same layout the `Qwen3VLMoe` / `Qwen3_5Moe` branch reads through `config.get_text_config()`. `Qwen4ExpTextConfig` is added alongside the architecture name so `--model-prefix text_config` also resolves, mirroring the existing `Qwen3_5MoeTextConfig` entry.\n\nAI assistance (Claude) was used to prepare this change; the diff was reviewed and the validation above was run by the submitter.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
